 ploads/organization/NKVE_1200x630_20260827192438781971.png
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Indivisible and Wake Up Sonoma are joining force
 s for a 'No Kings: Vote Early’ event on October 17. We need your support
  by showing up with your completed ballot. This will not be a protest. It 
 is all about marching to our local drop boxes for celebratory early ballot
  dropoff. The earlier we get those ballots in the safer our votes will be!
  TIME: 10am -12pm DATE: October 17th WHAT: JOIN US - to help us with get o
 ut the vote messaging in two different places: 1. In front of the Sono
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Regional Library\, 755 W Napa St\, Sonoma\, CA\, 95
 476
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/nokings/event/1056438/
X-SOURCE:Indivisible Sonoma County (Mobilize)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Become a Great Canvasser: How to Build Bridges to Voting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T170000
UID:9e325ebd3120fe7fdf60f2e67b89e413@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/event/Elizabeth%20Chur%20Canvass%20Curious%20Oct%202026%20Banner_20
 261001232020731288.png
DESCRIPTION:**Learn practical strategies for helping voters uncover their 
 reasons to vote for Democrats.** Some conversations are easy: the voter su
 pports your candidate\, they’re ready to vote\, and your job is pretty s
 traightforward. But what happens when someone is undecided or conflicted
 —or tells you\, “I don’t vote”? Join veteran canvassers and traine
 rs Elizabeth Chur—author of [The Joy of Talking Politics with Strangers]
 (https://elizabethchur.com/)—and Carol Blaney for this interactive one-h
 our workshop.
LOCATION:Virtual event
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/swingleft/event/1051113/
X-SOURCE:Indivisible Sonoma County (Mobilize)
END:VEVENT
